From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:24:06 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: Import from Another Browser works from the menu;
 every Meridian command is in its range
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Meridian's commands have no ActionItem, so BrowserCommandController supports
and enables them itself (IsMeridianCommand). That range was written by hand
and ended at IDC_MERIDIAN_ASK_PAGE (39728); IDC_MERIDIAN_IMPORT_OTHER (39729),
added for moving in from other browsers, fell outside it: the command updater
called it unsupported, so Meridian › Import from Another Browser… was greyed
out and did nothing in 1.5.2 and 1.5.3 (the command bar and the welcome tour
reach the same screen another way, which is why it went unnoticed).

The range is now IDC_MERIDIAN_FIRST..IDC_MERIDIAN_LAST next to the ids
(chrome_command_ids.h), checked in one place (meridian/commands.h), and
meridian_unittests reads chrome_command_ids.h and fails if any IDC_MERIDIAN_*
falls outside it or the range holds an id that isn't Meridian's.

Tests: meridian_unittests --gtest_filter=MeridianCommandsTest.*;
chromium/tests/browsers_import.test.mjs: the command itself (39729) opens the
moving-in step (it did nothing on the 1.5.3 build).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
